a deep rift in the republican party over  the january 6 attacks has once again  exploded into public view senate  minority leader mitch mcconnell has  rejected a republican party resolution  referring to those events on january 6  as quote legitimate political discourse  mcconnell says instead it was a quote  violent insurrection he also slammed the  rnc for censuring two republicans  investigating the attack nicole killian  has more now from washington  the highest ranking republican official  in the senate is making his stance clear  when it comes to the deadly january  sixth attack on the capitol it was a  violent insurrection for the purpose of  trying to prevent the peaceful transfer  of power tuesday senate minority leader  mitch mcconnell criticized the  republican national committee for  centering wyoming's liz cheney and  illinois adam kinzinger for serving on  the house select committee investigating  the insurrection  it was the language of the rnc  resolution to censure members of its own  party that struck a nerve stating that  cheney and kinzinger chose to join nancy  pelosi in a democrat-led persecution of  ordinary citizens who engaged in  legitimate political discourse but  members of the january 6 committee are  firing back ask the capitol police  officers  if  the people they interacted with were  engaged in legitimate  political discourse um it's just you  know at a human level it's just it's  just maddening  five people died after a pro-trump mob  breached the capitol building after  former president trump made repeated  false claims that the 2020 election was  stolen  rnc chair ronna mcdaniel claims the  party's position is being distorted and  wrote violence is not legitimate  political discourse whether in the u.s  capitol or in democrat-run cities across  the country the issue is  whether or not the rnc should be sort of  singling out  members of our party who may have  different views from the majority  that's not the job of the rnc  house minority leader kevin mccarthy has  dodged questions about the censure  resolution but conference chair elise  stefanik says the rnc has every right to  take any action now some house  republicans want cheney and kinzinger  expelled from the conference but she  told me that did not come up in their  meeting this week vlad  all right nicole killian for us on the  hill thank you very much
 

